WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.958
The cutaway follows one hook from the front of the lock.

00:00:00.958 --> 00:00:02.208
The hook meets resistance at pin 1.

00:00:02.208 --> 00:00:02.958
A groove catches. The blue driver still crosses the shear line.

00:00:02.958 --> 00:00:04.583
The core supports the driver at pin 1. Its lower pin can drop away.

00:00:04.583 --> 00:00:06.125
The lower pin has free play. The blue driver stays above it.

00:00:06.125 --> 00:00:06.458
The hook meets resistance at pin 2.

00:00:06.458 --> 00:00:06.917
A groove catches. The blue driver still crosses the shear line.

00:00:06.917 --> 00:00:07.375
A groove catches. The blue driver still crosses the shear line.

00:00:07.375 --> 00:00:08.083
A groove catches. The blue driver still crosses the shear line.

00:00:08.083 --> 00:00:08.833
The serrated driver clears. The picker takes this click for another groove and keeps lifting.

00:00:08.833 --> 00:00:09.875
The pale key pin is above the shear line. This catch comes from its notch.

00:00:09.875 --> 00:00:10.375
The hook is down. The notch holds the key pin up; the lock is still blocked.

00:00:10.375 --> 00:00:10.667
The picker eases the turning pressure. Watch the front driver as the trapped key pin comes free.

00:00:10.667 --> 00:00:11.208
The core has moved back under pin 1. Its spring pushes the driver down.

00:00:11.208 --> 00:00:11.750
The notch has slipped off the chamber edge. Pin 2 is back down.

00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:12.917
The lower pin is free. Pin 1 has also dropped and needs setting again.

00:00:12.917 --> 00:00:14.167
The hook meets resistance at pin 1.

00:00:14.167 --> 00:00:14.917
A groove catches. The blue driver still crosses the shear line.

00:00:14.917 --> 00:00:16.542
The core supports the driver at pin 1. Its lower pin can drop away.

00:00:16.542 --> 00:00:18.083
The lower pin has free play. The blue driver stays above it.

00:00:18.083 --> 00:00:19.333
The hook meets resistance at pin 2.

00:00:19.333 --> 00:00:20.083
A groove catches. The blue driver still crosses the shear line.

00:00:20.083 --> 00:00:21.708
The core supports the driver at pin 2. Its lower pin can drop away.

00:00:21.708 --> 00:00:23.125
The lower pin has free play. The blue driver stays above it.

00:00:23.125 --> 00:00:24.667
The lower pin has free play. The blue driver stays above it.

00:00:24.667 --> 00:00:25.458
